  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\nIssued at 1236 PM CDT SUN OCT 18 2026\n\nVery seasonable weather is expected for most of the next week, as\nupper-level ridging continues to slowly build off to our west.\nThis will still allow for afternoon highs to slowly climb a few\ndegrees, generally stabilizing in the mid-70s and low-80s by\nMidweek. Around this same timeframe, the flow aloft will begin to\ntransition into a rather interesting shape, as the ridge begins\nto get \"pinched\" by a deep trough to our west, and to our east.\nIn turn, we'll get placed into this north flow regime that will\nallow for cooler air to filter down the Appalachian mountain\nrange. Afternoon highs will generally be unaffected through the\nweek, but overnight lows will be slightly cooler for this time of\nthe year, as radiational cooling is expected from a lack of\nwinds. Closer towards next weekend, this north flow will slightly\nshift to the NE, which will then allow for our highs to take a\ndip. Under the influence of this NE flow, highs in the east will\nrange in the low-70s, where highs in the west will range in the\nupper-70s.\n\nGiven the ongoing lack of moisture depth in the air column\noverhead, and lack of a solid forcing mechanism, little to no\nrainfall is expected over the next seven days.\n\n/44/",
